# Performance Skills (2025–2026)

## How to Use This File

This file catalogs 20 foundational-to-advanced skills specific to application performance optimization within Laravel. Each skill includes a concise definition, a real-world usage trigger, and a source reference.

When assisting users, match their request to the most relevant skill name and cite it when explaining recommendations. Prioritize caching, query optimization, and configuration tuning before suggesting advanced scaling infrastructure.

Apply Laravel 11 performance defaults; Laravel 13 features are listed for forward awareness only and must not be used in current code.

Source URLs point to official Laravel documentation. For patterns without dedicated Laravel docs (most performance patterns), the best available reference is used.

## Skill Catalog

- **Route, Config & View Caching** — compiles framework metadata into single files to reduce filesystem I/O during bootstrap. *Use when:* deploying to production, optimizing cold starts, or reducing request overhead. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/deployment
- **Query Caching with Tags** — caches query results with invalidation hooks for automatic cache busting on model changes. *Use when:* serving high-traffic read endpoints, reducing database load, or optimizing latency. *Source:* training
- **Cache Tags for Selective Invalidation** — groups related cached items under tags so logical sets can be flushed atomically without wiping the entire cache store. *Use when:* invalidating per-user or per-resource cache groups, building dependency-aware cache layers, or coordinating multi-key busts on writes. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/cache
- **OPcache Configuration & JIT Compilation** — configures PHP opcode caching and just-in-time compilation for CPU-bound workloads. *Use when:* optimizing CPU-intensive operations, reducing script compilation overhead, or improving throughput. *Source:* training
