- **N+1 Lazy Loading Prevention** — uses `Model::preventLazyLoading()` to surface unoptimized relationship queries in development before they reach production. *Use when:* enforcing eager-loading discipline, catching N+1 patterns in CI, or hardening critical Eloquent code paths. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/eloquent-relationships
- **Eloquent vs Query Builder Tradeoffs** — chooses abstraction level based on readability, performance, and complexity requirements. *Use when:* optimizing critical paths, writing complex aggregations, or maintaining developer velocity. *Source:* training
- **Lazy Collections & Chunking** — processes records in memory-efficient streams to avoid out-of-memory errors. *Use when:* exporting reports, running background jobs, or handling large dataset imports. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/collections
- **Job Batching & Chain Coordination** — groups related jobs with progress tracking and callback handling for workflows. *Use when:* processing bulk imports, orchestrating multi-step operations, or enabling user progress. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/queues
- **Queue Worker Tuning** — configures worker processes, memory limits, and auto-restart policies for reliability. *Use when:* scaling background processing, preventing memory leaks, or ensuring consistent throughput. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/queues
- **Horizontal Scaling with Load Balancers** — distributes traffic across multiple app instances behind a reverse proxy. *Use when:* handling traffic spikes, improving fault tolerance, or enabling zero-downtime deployments. *Source:* training
- **Read Replicas for Query Offloading** — directs read queries to replica databases to reduce primary write contention. *Use when:* scaling read-heavy applications, improving report performance, or isolating analytical workloads. *Source:* training
- **Connection Pooling & Persistent Connections** — reuses database connections across requests to reduce handshake overhead. *Use when:* optimizing high-concurrency apps, reducing latency, or managing strict connection limits. *Source:* training
- **CDN Integration for Static Assets** — serves images, CSS, and JS from edge locations to reduce origin load. *Use when:* improving global performance, reducing bandwidth costs, or enabling cache strategies. *Source:* training
- **Image Optimization & Lazy Loading** — compresses, resizes, and defers image loading to improve perceived performance. *Use when:* building content-rich pages, supporting mobile users, or reducing bounce rates. *Source:* training
- **Response Caching & ETag Validation** — caches HTTP responses with entity tags to enable conditional request handling. *Use when:* serving cacheable API responses, reducing bandwidth, or improving client performance. *Source:* training
- **Laravel Octane Process Models** — uses Swoole, RoadRunner, or FrankenPHP to keep application in memory between requests. *Use when:* achieving sub-millisecond response times, reducing bootstrap overhead, or scaling efficiently. *Source:* https://laravel.com/docs/13.x/octane
- **Memory Leak Avoidance Patterns** — clears static caches, resets singletons, and avoids circular references in long-running processes. *Use when:* using Octane, processing large batches, or running background CLI daemons. *Source:* training
- **Cache::touch() TTL Extension (Laravel 13+)** — extends cache item lifetime without retrieving and re-storing values. *Use when:* implementing sliding expiration, optimizing cache hit rates, or reducing serialization overhead. *Source:* training
- **Vector Query Optimization (Laravel 13+)** — leverages pgvector indexes and similarity thresholds for efficient semantic search. *Use when:* building AI-powered search, recommendation engines, or content clustering at scale. *Source:* training

